  "title": "Sabidussi's compatibility conjecture",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "mediawiki-wikitext",
    "text": "Let ''G=(V,E)'' be an Eulerian graph with minimum degree at least 4, and let ''W'' be a closed Eulerian walk of ''G''. Is it true that ''G'' has a cycle decomposition such that no pair of consecutive edges of ''W'' appear in the same cycle of the decomposition?",
